WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:04.960
I spent 100 hours researching the wackiest
theories in One Piece - like the theory that

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:09.719
this dude is Luffy’s mother [Show Crocodile],
or the theory Luffy might die at the end of

00:00:10.742 --> 00:00:11.742
even more ridiculous than the mangaka Oda-Sensei
when they try to figure out what crazy plot

00:00:11.742 --> 00:00:12.742
twist is coming next!

00:00:12.742 --> 00:00:14.983
But here’s an absurd sounding theory that…might
actually make sense?

00:00:14.983 --> 00:00:19.623
The first rival devil fruit user that Luffy
ever fought against was Buggy the Clown all

00:00:19.623 --> 00:00:21.843
the way back in the beginning chapters of
One Piece.

00:00:21.843 --> 00:00:26.133
Buggy the Chop-Chop fruit user was revealed
to have known Luffy’s mentor Shanks as a

00:00:26.133 --> 00:00:31.852
child and even served alongside him as a cabin
boy on Gol D. Roger&nbsp; the pirate king’s

00:00:31.852 --> 00:00:32.852
ship!

00:00:32.852 --> 00:00:36.573
Throughout the whole series, as Luffy has
fought tooth and nail to get stronger, Buggy

00:00:36.573 --> 00:00:38.863
has been failing upwards.

00:00:38.863 --> 00:00:42.543
After Luffy teamed up with him to break out
of the prison Impel Down, Buggy was named

00:00:42.543 --> 00:00:44.722
a Warlord of the Sea by the World Government.

00:00:44.722 --> 00:00:48.852
And now he’s even become an Emperor of the
Sea!

00:00:48.852 --> 00:00:53.563
But if Buggy keeps accidentally stumbling
into higher and higher positions in the pirate

00:00:53.563 --> 00:00:58.563
world, there’s only one more place to go
after being named a Yonkou.

00:00:58.563 --> 00:01:03.773
That’s right - even though Luffy will be
the one to deserve the title of pirate king,

00:01:03.773 --> 00:01:08.642
is it possible that the world will recognize
Buggy as the pirate king first??

00:01:08.642 --> 00:01:09.642
**#2 - Portgas D. Rouge ate the Gomu-Gomu
no Mi**

00:01:09.642 --> 00:01:14.163
In all my research, though, that theory doesn’t
even come close to the craziest.

00:01:14.163 --> 00:01:19.723
That’s right - there are ten more theories
even crazier than Buggy becoming King of the

00:01:19.723 --> 00:01:20.723
Pirates!

00:01:20.723 --> 00:01:24.633
This next one deals with who had Luffy’s
Gomu-Gomu no Mi before Luffy did.

00:01:24.633 --> 00:01:27.803
Lots of people assumed for a long time that
it must have been Roger.

00:01:27.803 --> 00:01:32.282
After all, Roger shares a dream with Luffy,
he was the original owner of the Straw Hat,

00:01:32.282 --> 00:01:34.943
and has a really similar personality to Luffy.

00:01:34.943 --> 00:01:39.182
So it would only make sense if Roger even
had the Gomu-Gomu no Mi.

00:01:39.182 --> 00:01:45.523
But this theory says it’s not Roger at all,
but Portgas D. Rouge who previously had this

00:01:45.523 --> 00:01:46.523
rubber power.

00:01:46.523 --> 00:01:51.243
For those of you who need a reminder, Rouge
is Luffy’s brother Ace’s mother.

00:01:51.243 --> 00:01:56.553
She’s notable for having been pregnant with
Ace for 2 years before giving birth.

00:01:56.553 --> 00:02:01.043
Since the government was rounding up any baby
that could have been Roger’s offspring,

00:02:01.043 --> 00:02:06.273
she somehow kept Ace in her womb for fifteen
extra months.

00:02:06.273 --> 00:02:07.523
How is this possible?

00:02:07.523 --> 00:02:15.043
Well, according to this theory, she did it
because she had a….really stretchy uterus?

00:02:15.043 --> 00:02:20.092
Now I know that Oda’s series isn’t exactly
scientifically accurate, especially when it

00:02:20.092 --> 00:02:25.092
comes to the medical field…but this one
seems like a “stretch” in more ways than

00:02:25.092 --> 00:02:26.092
one.

00:02:26.092 --> 00:02:27.092
**#3 - The fight against the Blackbeard Pirates
will be a Davy Back Fight**

00:02:27.092 --> 00:02:29.633
Now we all know that Goda is a master of foreshadowing.

00:02:29.633 --> 00:02:33.223
Therefore he’d never put anything in his
series that wasn’t relevant!

00:02:33.223 --> 00:02:39.203
So what was with the Davy Back Fight arc where
the Straw Hats competed with Foxy on Long

00:02:39.203 --> 00:02:40.402
Ring Long Land?

00:02:40.402 --> 00:02:47.923
It’s an arc so disliked by some fans that
some people mistakenly think it’s filler!

00:02:47.923 --> 00:02:51.182
But nope, this is a canon manga arc.

00:02:51.182 --> 00:02:55.013
So will Davy Back Fights become important
again?

00:02:55.013 --> 00:02:59.533
Well, some people think that it will come
back in a big way when the Straw Hats finally

00:02:59.533 --> 00:03:04.913
go head on against the Blackbeard Pirates!

00:03:04.913 --> 00:03:09.663
Every One Piece theorist out there has their
dream matchups of which Straw Hat will fight

00:03:09.663 --> 00:03:15.383
which Blackbeard Pirate - so imagine the God
Tier Troll that Oda could pull when Marshall

00:03:15.383 --> 00:03:19.353
D. Teach challenges Luffy to this high-stakes,
ridiculous game!

00:03:19.353 --> 00:03:22.923
**#4 - The Thousand Sunny is Pluton**

00:03:22.923 --> 00:03:27.083
Cyborg Franky, the shipwright of the Straw
Hats, built the Thousand Sunny after their

00:03:27.083 --> 00:03:32.473
old ship the Going Merry finally had to be
retired after being terribly damaged in many

00:03:32.473 --> 00:03:33.643
voyages.

00:03:33.643 --> 00:03:38.023
But before he built this ship, it was revealed
that Franky had hidden the blueprints to the

00:03:38.023 --> 00:03:42.703
Ancient Weapon Pluton, an all-powerful warship,
for decades.

00:03:42.703 --> 00:03:47.572
He even went to far as to burn the blueprints
to protect them from falling into the hands

00:03:47.572 --> 00:03:49.503
of the World Government.

00:03:49.503 --> 00:03:55.352
But with his technological genius, what if
he transferred part of the designs into his

00:03:55.352 --> 00:03:56.432
dream ship?

00:03:56.432 --> 00:04:00.762
Is The Thousand Sunny hiding some crazy weaponry?

00:04:00.762 --> 00:04:05.143
Is Oda finally going to give us the ship-to-ship
combat we’ve always dreamed of??

00:04:05.143 --> 00:04:07.333
**#5 - Imu and the Gorosei are immortal because
of the immortality surgery**

00:04:07.333 --> 00:04:12.423
Now these next three theories are all related
and they deal with one of the most theorized

00:04:12.423 --> 00:04:14.942
about powers in all of One Piece.

00:04:14.942 --> 00:04:19.743
In Dressrosa, Donquixote Doflamingo revealed
a secret power of the Ope-Ope no Mi - the

00:04:19.743 --> 00:04:21.733
fruit used by Trafalgar Law.

00:04:21.733 --> 00:04:26.942
Apparently the fruit’s Immortality Surgery
can sacrifice the user’s life in order to

00:04:26.942 --> 00:04:29.383
grant someone immortality.

00:04:29.383 --> 00:04:34.593
Dofllamingo wanted Law to use the power on
him, but thankfully Luffy saved the day and

00:04:34.593 --> 00:04:36.752
defeated the warlord.

00:04:36.752 --> 00:04:41.303
Viewers have noticed, though, that a certain
set of characters always appear to be the

00:04:41.303 --> 00:04:45.123
same age even when they appear in flashbacks.

00:04:45.123 --> 00:04:50.053
Usually when we flashback 20 years or so to
see younger versions of Rayleigh or Garp or

00:04:50.053 --> 00:04:55.443
whatever other character, it’s very clear
that they’ve aged.

00:04:55.443 --> 00:05:01.663
However, the Five Elder Stars always appear
to look exactly the same.

00:05:01.663 --> 00:05:05.733
We can also guess that the same is true for
the secret leader of the World Government,

00:05:05.733 --> 00:05:06.733
Imu-Sama.

00:05:06.733 --> 00:05:12.442
Did several previous users of the Ope-Ope
no Mi sacrifice themselves to give the rulers

00:05:12.442 --> 00:05:14.463
of the government everlasting life?

00:05:14.463 --> 00:05:20.263
If so, it would make sense that Doflamingo,
a Celestial Dragon, would know about the power.

00:05:20.263 --> 00:05:21.263
**#6.

00:05:21.263 --> 00:05:22.263
Law will make Luffy immortal with the surgery**

00:05:22.263 --> 00:05:27.092
Law having this crazy power at all, though,
begs the question: Who’s he going to use

00:05:27.092 --> 00:06:22.782
the Immortality Surgery on?

00:06:22.782 --> 00:06:27.883
It would be a crime against storytelling to
introduce such an earth-shattering power and

00:06:27.883 --> 00:06:30.733
have it never be relevant to the story!

00:06:30.733 --> 00:06:35.912
Well, one obvious person for him to use it
on would be Straw Hat Luffy himself.

00:06:35.912 --> 00:06:41.312
Ever since the time skip, Law has been Luffy’s
greatest ally in the ongoing conflict against

00:06:41.312 --> 00:06:44.043
Doflamingo, Kaidou, and Big Mom.

00:06:44.043 --> 00:06:48.993
And while the two are rivals for the One Piece,
one could definitely imagine a scenario where

00:06:48.993 --> 00:06:54.363
Luffy’s life is threatened, so Law sacrifices
himself to save his ally.

00:06:54.363 --> 00:06:59.733
It would be absolutely heart wrenching, and
possibly the saddest death in the entire series.

00:06:59.733 --> 00:07:05.883
After all, we’ve spent a lot more time with
Law than we ever did with Ace or Whitebeard.

00:07:05.883 --> 00:07:06.883
What do you think?

00:07:06.883 --> 00:07:10.683
After all the fake out deaths we’ve had,
do you think Oda would be bold enough to kill

00:07:10.683 --> 00:07:12.293
off a fan favorite like Law??

00:07:12.293 --> 00:07:13.293
**#7 - Luffy Will Die**

00:07:13.293 --> 00:07:18.673
And speaking of killing off characters, here’s
the most controversial one Oda could possibly

00:07:18.673 --> 00:07:19.673
kill.

00:07:19.673 --> 00:07:22.463
At the end of the series, will Luffy die?

00:07:22.463 --> 00:07:27.972
Let’s say that Law doesn’t make the ultimate
sacrifice to make Luffy immortal…we hate

00:07:27.972 --> 00:07:33.183
to say it, but Luffy has some death flags.

00:07:33.183 --> 00:07:35.023
First off, he wants to be the pirate king.

00:07:35.023 --> 00:07:39.812
And we all know what happened to the last
pirate king…a little thing called public

00:07:39.812 --> 00:07:41.053
execution.

00:07:41.053 --> 00:07:45.853
Maybe Luffy’s death will be what sets off
a brand new pirate era.

00:07:45.853 --> 00:07:51.153
Secondly, though, just think of all the time
that it’s been hinted that Luffy is shortening

00:07:51.153 --> 00:07:52.562
his life span.

00:07:52.562 --> 00:07:56.823
When he uses Gear 2 for the first time in
Enies Lobby, CP9 hints that such a technique

00:07:56.823 --> 00:07:59.673
would be shortening his life overall.

00:07:59.673 --> 00:08:04.243
When he received hormone treatments from Ivankov,
Iva also warned that it would take years off

00:08:04.243 --> 00:08:05.912
his life.

00:08:05.912 --> 00:08:10.812
Recently during the Kaidou fight, after using
Gear 5 for a while, Luffy appeared to transform

00:08:10.812 --> 00:08:13.733
into an elderly man temporarily.

00:08:13.733 --> 00:08:17.323
Just how much lifespan does Luffy have left
to shorten??

00:08:17.323 --> 00:08:18.812
**#8 -&nbsp; Crocodile is Luffy’s Mom**

00:08:18.812 --> 00:08:23.833
Ah, we’re finally back to CrocoMom - the
theory we hinted at the beginning of the video.

00:08:23.833 --> 00:08:27.603
But wait a minute, this is only #8 of 11 theories!

00:08:27.603 --> 00:08:31.903
You mean there are 3 more theories even wilder
than this?

00:08:31.903 --> 00:08:34.913
Oh yeah, so you’ll just have to stay tuned.

00:08:34.913 --> 00:08:36.963
But first - here’s CrocoMom.

00:08:36.963 --> 00:08:43.163
Now this is one of the longest running, most
memeified, and weirdly believable theories

00:08:43.163 --> 00:08:45.023
in the entire fanbase.

00:08:45.023 --> 00:08:46.493
When Luffy helped Crocodile and co.

00:08:46.493 --> 00:08:52.523
break out of Impel Down, Emporio Ivankov convinced
this former warlord to be on his best behavior

00:08:52.523 --> 00:08:55.422
by holding some deep dark secret over him.

00:08:55.422 --> 00:09:00.543
Given that the person who knows Croc’s secret
is Ivankov, who can notably change peoples’

00:09:00.543 --> 00:09:06.313
genders with their hormone fruit, it’s heavily
speculated that Crocodile was actually born

00:09:06.313 --> 00:09:10.383
a woman and asked Iva to turn into a man.

00:09:10.383 --> 00:09:15.343
This fan theory takes this speculation one
step further, though, and suggests that not

00:09:15.343 --> 00:09:16.982
only was Crocodile a woman.

00:09:16.982 --> 00:09:19.042
She’s actually Luffy’s mom.

00:09:19.042 --> 00:09:24.693
After all, Oda has stated that Luffy’s mom
is a character he’s drawn before…so this

00:09:24.693 --> 00:09:26.333
guess seems as good as any!

00:09:26.333 --> 00:09:27.403
**#9 -. The crew will go to the Moon**

00:09:27.403 --> 00:09:32.362
For our final three One Piece theories you
didn’t know existed, we have theories about

00:09:32.362 --> 00:09:34.153
the One Piece itself.

00:09:34.153 --> 00:09:39.563
Theory #9 is that the One Piece isn’t in
the Grand Line at all…it’s on the moon!

00:09:39.563 --> 00:09:44.893
Listen, I promise this has more to it than
you think!

00:09:44.893 --> 00:09:50.253
If you’re an anime only watcher, you might
not realize just how important the moon is

00:09:50.253 --> 00:09:52.052
to the story of One Piece.

00:09:52.052 --> 00:09:58.052
In the manga, Oda often uses his cover pages
to tell side stories about what characters

00:09:58.052 --> 00:10:00.783
are up to around the world.

00:10:00.783 --> 00:10:06.553
After Skypiea, we got to see Enel fulfill
his dream of traveling to “Fairy Vearth”

00:10:06.553 --> 00:10:08.623
AKA the moon.

00:10:08.623 --> 00:10:13.723
What was shocking was that the moon was actually
inhabited!

00:10:13.723 --> 00:10:17.763
Enel ran into alien Space Pirates and an army
of automatons.

00:10:17.763 --> 00:10:22.383
He even found the ruins of an ancient civilization
that would appear to depict the winged races

00:10:22.383 --> 00:10:27.713
of the Sky Island together with images of
the ancient weapons.

00:10:27.713 --> 00:10:33.323
If the moon is connected to some mysterious
ancient civilization, could it be possible

00:10:33.323 --> 00:10:37.533
that the greatest treasure - the One Piece
- is there too?

00:10:37.533 --> 00:10:38.533
**10.

00:10:38.533 --> 00:10:40.612
The One Piece is the friends we made along
the way**

00:10:40.612 --> 00:10:41.612
Another popular One Piece theory?

00:10:41.612 --> 00:10:42.612
It’s nothing.

00:10:42.612 --> 00:10:43.813
There is no treasure at all.

00:10:43.813 --> 00:10:48.623
Now this theory is practically as old as the
entire series, with fans constantly joking

00:10:48.623 --> 00:10:53.763
that the One Piece would be “the adventure
itself” or “the friends we made along

00:10:53.763 --> 00:10:54.763
the way.”

00:10:54.763 --> 00:10:58.732
Oda has stated that the One Piece is a physical
treasure.

00:10:58.732 --> 00:11:03.763
But knowing how hard Oda can troll, we wouldn’t
put it past him for that physical treasure

00:11:03.763 --> 00:11:08.763
to be a written note from Roger that says…that
the real treasure is friendship.

00:11:08.763 --> 00:11:13.213
I know a few fans who would probably drop
the series if this were true…but the joke

00:11:13.213 --> 00:11:17.112
would be on them because the series would
already be over.

00:11:17.112 --> 00:11:22.063
But I highly doubt Oda would let us down - instead
the One Piece treasure will probably be something

00:11:22.063 --> 00:11:24.633
completely awesome.

00:11:24.633 --> 00:11:25.633
Something like:

00:11:25.633 --> 00:11:26.633
**11.

00:11:26.633 --> 00:11:27.633
Luffy will destroy the red line**

00:11:27.633 --> 00:11:31.203
The One Piece is Luffy destroying the red
line - the massive continent that circles

00:11:31.203 --> 00:11:35.423
the globe and separates the planet into four
distinct oceans.

00:11:35.423 --> 00:11:39.302
But wait - how is destroying the red line
a treasure?

00:11:39.302 --> 00:11:45.813
Well, this would very literally make the world
into “one piece” by uniting all four oceans

00:11:45.813 --> 00:11:46.813
into one.

00:11:46.813 --> 00:11:51.203
A couple big hints for this theory are that
Marie Jois, the capital of the world government,

00:11:51.203 --> 00:11:53.683
is located on top of the Red Line.

00:11:53.683 --> 00:11:58.583
If Luffy ends up going to war against the
World Government and takes the fight to them,

00:11:58.583 --> 00:12:03.672
destroying Pangea Castle might result in destroying
the Red Line, too.

00:12:03.672 --> 00:12:08.203
In addition, when the crew was on Fishman
Island, the fortune teller Madame Sharly prophesied

00:12:08.203 --> 00:12:11.133
that Luffy would destroy the island.

00:12:11.133 --> 00:12:18.802
And Fishman Island happens to be located beneath
the Red Line, directly below Marie Jois.

00:12:18.802 --> 00:12:22.823
We also have hints such as the whale Laboon,
the first character we met in the Grand Line,

00:12:22.823 --> 00:12:27.373
repeatedly bashing his head against the Red
Line, trying to destroy it.

00:12:27.373 --> 00:12:31.953
Bringing down the Red Line would mean uniting
the world and bringing the people together

00:12:31.953 --> 00:12:34.802
into one people - One Piece.

00:12:34.802 --> 00:12:35.802
**Conclusion**

00:12:35.802 --> 00:12:39.253
These were just 11 of the wildest One Piece
theories that I found after doing tons and

00:12:39.253 --> 00:12:40.362
tons of research.

00:12:40.362 --> 00:12:45.033
I just discussed this one about Oars being
the original Joy Boy, that will blow your

00:12:45.033 --> 00:12:46.033
mind.

00:12:46.033 --> 00:12:48.542
So if you have some more time, go check it
out here.

